      "Language": "ukr",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The study is based on clinical examination of movement disorder in 126 patients (men--103, women--23) with lumbosacral pain syndrome. The authors revealed how statico-dynamic and neurotic disorders had been formed depending on structural peculiarities of primary pathologic process and thus determining different clinical forms. Mechanisms of syndromologic manifestation of suffering in every case were substantiated; own approaches to anatomico-topical diagnostics and objectification of pathology course in dynamic were suggested."},
